# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),
and each of the three versions adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

A release is a tag: `kernel-X.Y.Z`, `ocaml-X.Y.Z` or `py-X.Y.Z`.

## Kernel

The Rocq theories and their extraction in `ocaml/kernel`.  A release is
listed under the djot syntax reference it implements; moving to a newer
reference is at least a minor release.

### [Unreleased]
- list, ordered list and definition list uniformity hold for items of any lines when keys are off: `list_uniformity_shape`, `ordered_uniformity_shape`, `definition_list_uniformity_shape`
- `Reached.v`: states a run reaches, and that a blank line after them changes no block (`reached_blank_finish`)
- a blank line at the end of the input changes no block when keys are off: `trailing_blank_line`
- the same list uniformity for a list closed by a blank and a following line, when the last item does not end inside an attribute spec: `list_uniformity_shape_tail`
- holes extension (`ext_holes`): `` %`e` ``, a code span with a `%` before it, is a `Hole` holding the span's content, read as math's `` $`e` `` is; a hole's text, for identifiers and labels, is its expression
- the candidate stack holds link destinations only

{syntax-reference-commit="d77f8a0cbea6785c42b3e2b03463195b5ca6f7c7"}
### djot 2026-06-16
#### [0.1.0]
- initial release with extensions: callouts, custom tags, dollar math, keyed blocks, list interruption, setext heading, wikilinks
- djot syntax reference partially done

## OCaml package

The `djot` opam package in `ocaml/`: the library, `djot.json` and the CLI.
A new kernel is a new release of the package.

### [Unreleased]
- `Doc.source_blocks`: the blocks without the identifiers derived from heading text, for `Doc.make` to give the same document
- `Profile.with_ext_holes` and `Inline.Hole`: holes, `` %`e` ``
- `Mapper.holes_as_raw`: each hole as a raw inline in format `hole`, which `` `e`{=hole} `` also reads as

### [0.1.0]
- initial release, with kernel 0.1.0

## Python package

`djotv` in `py/`.  A new kernel is a new release of the package.

### [Unreleased]
- `ast.ExtHole` and the `ext_holes` switch: holes, `` %`e` ``

### [0.1.0]
- initial release, with kernel 0.1.0
